 ### [Sparse Volume Texture Setup](7432-sparse-volume-texture-setup.md)
-Sparse Volume Texture (SVT) setup is a method for rendering large volumetric datasets in Unreal Engine 5 by storing data in sparse tiles within a single large volume texture, circumventing the DirectX 12 API limit of 2048 voxels per dimension. It solves the problem of contiguous memory fragmentation limiting single texture allocation to ~1 gigavoxel in earlier approaches, allowing the display of massive datasets (up to ~6 gigavoxels) at reasonable frame rates by accepting chunked rendering. Unlike a single contiguous texture which avoids lighting discontinuities but exceeds allocation limits, SVT enables the display of entire massive datasets by treating a collection of sparse tiles as a single logical volume.
+Sparse Volume Texture (SVT) setup is a method for rendering large volumetric datasets in Unreal Engine 5 by storing data in sparse tiles within a single large volume texture, circumventing the DirectX 12 API limit of 2048 voxels per dimension. It solves the problem of contiguous memory fragmentation limiting single texture allocation to approximately 1 gigavoxel in earlier approaches, allowing the display of massive datasets (up to ~6 gigavoxels) at reasonable frame rates by treating a collection of sparse tiles as a single logical volume. Unlike a single contiguous texture which avoids lighting discontinuities but exceeds allocation limits, SVT enables the display of entire massive datasets without chunking artifacts.
 
 ### Texture Setup
-This variant focuses on loading 2D textures for procedural effects or shadow maps in WebGPU environments. It involves loading a texture from a file (e.g., `./LDR_LLL1_16.png`), creating a sampler with specific address modes ("repeat" for U and V) and filter modes ("nearest" for mag, min, and mipmap), and configuring the texture with usages for both rendering and binding [S3, unofficial]. The texture is created with a size of 512x512 and format "depth32float" or "rgba8unorm" depending on the purpose [S3, unofficial].
